# Kept small on purpose: the build stage copies the whole workspace, so anything not excluded
# here is sent to the daemon and can end up in a layer.
node_modules
**/node_modules
dist
**/dist
build
**/build
.vite
**/.vite
coverage
**/coverage

# ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# Secrets must never reach an image (FR-041).
#
# **`**/` IS LOAD-BEARING, and its absence was a real leak.** Docker matches these patterns with
# `filepath.Match` semantics, in which `*` does not cross `/` — so a bare `.env` matches only the
# context root. 006 builds the API image ON THE VM with `context: ../..` (deploy/vm/
# docker-compose.yml), i.e. the directory that also contains `deploy/vm/.env` — that environment's
# POSTGRES_PASSWORD, AUTH_PASSWORD_PEPPER and AUTH_ATTEMPT_HASH_KEY — and `deploy/vm/backups`,
# up to seven `pg_dump` archives of the live database. Neither was excluded, and the build stage
# is `COPY . .`, so every deploy baked both into a build-stage layer that `docker image prune -f`
# does not remove.
# ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
.env
.env.*
**/.env
**/.env.*
!.env.example
!**/.env.example

# The database's own backups, and the built client. Neither belongs in an API image, and the
# first is every attendee row and every credential hash.
deploy/vm/backups
**/backups
deploy/vm/web

.git
.github
.githooks
.specify
.claude

# Not the API's concern, and the largest directories in the repository.
GroundZero
specs
brainstorm
e2e
playwright-report
test-results
blob-report

*.log
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
